# Edge function deploys — clean tree + commit SHA

## Rule

Every Edge Function deploy must:

1. Run from a **clean git working tree** (no staged/unstaged/untracked changes that belong in the deploy). Refuse to deploy if `git status --porcelain` is non-empty.
2. Record the **full commit SHA** (`git rev-parse HEAD`) in the deploy log / report.

Use `scripts/deploy-edge-function.sh <slug>` (or the same checks inline). Do not `supabase functions deploy` from a dirty tree.

## Do not

- Deploy uncommitted local edits “just to smoke”
- Deploy without stating the commit SHA in the agent report
